-- Re-apply the new-style daily words for 14–20 Nov. 0043 matched on the exact old text, which can miss;
-- this matches any day that is still in the old one-paragraph style (no line breaks), so edits already in the new style are kept.

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = 'Israel had a habit of forgetting. They sang and danced on the banks of the Red Sea, and three days later they were complaining about water. God had not stopped working. They had stopped remembering.

Memory matters in the life of faith. When today''s problem looks big, yesterday''s testimony reminds you who you are dealing with. The God who carried you through that hospital visit, that exam, that season with no money, has not changed.

That is why the psalmist says God made His works "to be remembered". Your testimonies are not just old stories. They are evidence, kept for days like this one.

Today: write down three things God has done for you. Keep the list where you will see it the next time worry knocks.',
  declaration = 'I will not forget what God has done for me. My testimonies are proof that He will not fail me now.',
  prayer = 'Father, forgive me for the times I let one problem erase my memory of Your goodness. Bring back to my mind the ways You have carried me. When worry rises today, let my testimonies speak louder than my fear. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy318' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = 'David had watched eagles rise on the wind, strong and unhurried, high above everything below. He uses that picture to describe what God does for a tired soul.

Many of us are running on empty and trying to fill up on the wrong things: more scrolling, more busyness, more approval from people. None of it satisfies for long. Psalm 103 says it is the Lord who satisfies you with good things. Not things that only keep you busy, but things that actually feed you.

Renewal is not something you manufacture by trying harder. It is something you receive when you come close to the Source. A few quiet minutes with God can do what hours of distraction cannot.

Today: notice what you reach for when you feel empty. Next time, pause and reach for God first, even with one sentence of prayer.',
  declaration = 'I will not run on empty. God is my source, and He is renewing my strength today.',
  prayer = 'Lord, I confess that I often look for satisfaction in things that leave me emptier. Teach me to come to You first. Where I am tired, fill me again. Where I am dry, satisfy me with what is truly good, and lift me up today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy319' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = 'Ashes are what is left when something has burned down. A plan that failed. A relationship that ended. A dream you buried quietly. Most of us know what it is to sit in ashes.

Isaiah describes a God who does not leave us there. He makes an exchange. He takes ashes and gives beauty. He takes mourning and gives joy. He takes the heavy spirit that makes it hard to get out of bed, and gives a garment of praise to wear instead.

Notice the word "garment". Praise is something you put on, often before you feel like it. As you wear it, something begins to shift on the inside.

And God''s purpose is bigger than your recovery. He wants you planted, rooted and growing, so that your life shows others how good He is.

Today: name one "ash" in your life and hand it to God in prayer. Then put on praise, even if it starts with one song.',
  declaration = 'My story does not end in ashes. God is turning my pain into something beautiful, and my life will bring Him glory.',
  prayer = 'Father, You see the places in my life that have burned down. I will not hide them from You. I give You my disappointment and my grief, and I receive what You offer in exchange. Help me choose praise today, even before I feel it. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy320' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = 'The Book of Psalms ends with a simple instruction: if you have breath, praise the Lord. Not if you have a good voice, a perfect week or a full bank account. Just breath.

That means the qualification for praise is something you already have. You did not earn this morning''s breath, and you cannot hold the next one in your hand. Every single one is a gift.

We often wait to praise until something good happens. The Psalms teach us to praise first. Praise is not a reward we give God for answering us. It is the right response to who He is, and it lifts our eyes from what we lack to the One who holds everything.

Today: take five slow breaths. With each one, thank God for something specific. Let your breathing become worship.',
  declaration = 'As long as I have breath, I have a reason to praise. My praise does not wait for my circumstances to change.',
  prayer = 'Lord, thank You for this breath and the one after it. Forgive me for the days I took life for granted and kept my praise waiting for a better moment. I choose to honour You now, just as I am. Let my whole day be a song to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy321' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = '"Make a joyful noise." Some of us are glad the Bible did not say "make a beautiful sound". God is not asking for a performance. He is inviting you to come close with a glad heart.

Notice how this psalm tells us to come: with thanksgiving. Thanksgiving is the door into God''s presence. When you begin by thanking Him, your focus moves from your problems to His goodness, and your heart opens up to worship.

Worship is not only for Sunday morning. It can happen in the kitchen, on the bus, in the middle of traffic. Wherever you lift your heart to Him, that place becomes a place of His presence.

Today: before you ask God for anything, spend two minutes only thanking Him. Then sing one song, out loud if you can.',
  declaration = 'I am not a spectator. I am a worshipper, and wherever I go today, I carry thanksgiving in my heart.',
  prayer = 'Lord, I don''t want to come to You only with requests. Today I come with thanks. Fill my heart with gladness, and let my home, my work and my journey be filled with the sound of praise. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy322' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = 'Psalm 77 does not begin with joy. It begins with a man who cannot sleep, who feels forgotten by God and asks, "Will the Lord cast off for ever?" If you have ever felt like that, you are in good company.

But halfway through, something changes. Asaph makes a decision: "I will remember." He does not wait to feel better. He turns his mind, on purpose, to what God has done: the Red Sea, the wilderness, the way God led His people like a flock.

Your feelings are real, but they are not the whole story. When you cannot see God''s hand today, look back at where His hand has been. Remembering is how faith finds its feet again.

Today: tell someone about a time God came through for you. Saying it out loud strengthens your faith, and it may strengthen theirs.',
  declaration = 'My feelings do not have the final word. God has been faithful before, and He will be faithful again.',
  prayer = 'Father, some nights I struggle to feel You near. In those moments, help me choose to remember. Remind me of every time You made a way. Turn my questions into worship, and let my story encourage someone else today. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy323' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;

UPDATE devotions SET reflection = '"With my whole heart." Not half of it, while the other half worries about bills. Not the part left over after everything else. David chose to give God all of it.

Wholehearted praise spills over into our words. David says, "I will shew forth all thy marvellous works." When God has been good to you, you cannot keep quiet about it. A testimony is simply praise that other people can hear.

Many people around you are carrying heavy burdens and have never heard how God can help. Your story, told simply and honestly, could be the first light they see.

Today: share one thing God has done for you, with a friend, in a message or on your status. Keep it short and real, and let Him use it.',
  declaration = 'I will not keep God''s goodness to myself. My life and my words point people to Him.',
  prayer = 'Most High, I give You my whole heart today, not just a part of it. Give me courage to speak about Your goodness, and lead me to someone who needs to hear it. Let my joy point them to You. In Jesus'' name, Amen.'
WHERE id = 'dy324' AND instr(reflection, char(10)) = 0;
